      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "process Process_CopyOutMaterialized",
      "prov:value": "A process whose omission looks exactly like compliance is the vlhk shape, and advisory would not hold it.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean vlhk"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "library/processes/copy-out-materialized.bpmn#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "lane Lane_Reader",
      "prov:value": "ANY reader, and that is a ruling rather than an oversight — the owner, 2026-09-22, chose it over restricting the copy-out to an editor. Refusing a copy would not protect the original, because the original is protected by being read-only; a permission here would only stop people working.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-22"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-22"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "library/processes/copy-out-materialized.bpmn#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "lane Lane_Folio",
      "prov:value": "Where the copy lands, chosen by the owner 2026-09-22 over a scratch area. A scratch area lost because it makes the copy publishable by accident: a directory nobody declared is a directory nobody gates.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-22"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-22"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "library/processes/copy-out-materialized.bpmn#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "serviceTask Task_RecordProvenance",
      "prov:value": "A copy-out writes `local`; it does not overwrite `upstream`, and it does not reuse `upstream` for a local value — that was one field until 2026-09-22, and by then 5 of the 9 who-iris item records were using it for a local one in violation of its own documentation. Without `local`, one rename later the copy is indistinguishable from original work and nothing downstream can repair it, because the information was never written down.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-22"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-22"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "library/processes/copy-out-materialized.bpmn#provenance-5",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "file header comment",
      "prov:value": "Bean: folio-assistant-10s1.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean folio-assistant-10s1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "library/processes/copy-out-materialized.bpmn#provenance-6",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "process Process_CopyOutMaterialized",
      "prov:value": "Materialized content is read-only. The owner, 2026-09-21: &quot;if we have a materialized &lt;stub&gt;/&lt;sub-graph&gt;, the contents of it should be immutable ... you would need to copy/mateiralize it to your own folio/ in order to mess around with it.&quot; And 2026-09-22, choosing between advising and enforcing: enforce from the start.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-21",
        "2026-09-22"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-21",
        "2026-09-22"
